      "rows": [
        {
          "dimension": "Smart-contract security",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "A $11.1M exploit in March 2024 was followed by the Resupply team discovering multiple additional high-severity bugs in the contracts during the shutdown audit, and a community dev review concluded the hack was 'the inevitable consequence of the team behavior regarding security.'",
          "source": "https://rekt.news/prismafi-rekt"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Centralization",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "The emergency multisig unilaterally paused the entire protocol immediately after the exploit, and the hacker's demand that the founding team publicly dox themselves exposed how small and identifiable the control structure was.",
          "source": "https://hackmd.io/@PrismaRisk/PostMortem0328"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Oracle / MEV exposure",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "PrismaRisk's historical analysis found that choosing the Curve Oracle over the deployed oracle would have reduced MEV extraction by bots and improved exchange rates for users, indicating the oracle selection was a material and avoidable risk factor.",
          "source": "https://hackmd.io/@PrismaRisk/PostMortem0328"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Governance",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Post-exploit governance (fee pause, 50% emissions cut, PIP-038 repayment plan, and eventual shutdown vote) showed the DAO could mobilize rapidly but that all critical decisions were made reactively under duress rather than through proactive risk management.",
          "source": "https://hackmd.io/@PrismaRisk/PostMortem0328"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Liquidity",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Sequential protocol pauses, proposed fee increases mirroring MakerDAO's 5% mint fee or 15% interest rate model, and a 50% cut to emissions progressively eroded LP and mkUSD/ULTRA holder incentives ahead of the eventual shutdown.",
          "source": "https://iq.wiki/wiki/prisma-finance-mkusd"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Collateral / LSD-LRT risk",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "PrismaRisk flagged sfrxETH as promising but still-evolving collateral; the subsequent ULTRA expansion into liquid restaking tokens added newer, less battle-tested collateral categories shortly before the protocol was shut down.",
          "source": "https://thedefiant.io/news/defi/prisma-introduces-ultra-stablecoin-backed-by-liquid-restaking-tokens"
        }
